11
00:00:24,958 --> 00:00:31,625
[INTRO PLAYS]

12
00:00:31,625 --> 00:00:32,625
Subtitles: TAFFYMARZI

13
00:00:35,041 --> 00:00:38,000
It's time for Cake at Stake
for the team that lost last time.

14
00:00:38,500 --> 00:00:41,791
Even though they were in first place for a while,
Coiny's team came in last.

15
00:00:42,208 --> 00:00:44,958
So let's go Coiny, Icy, and Needy.

16
00:00:47,583 --> 00:00:49,791
We got eighteen votes. A record high!

17
00:00:50,166 --> 00:00:52,083
So, yeah. I've got two halves of a cake.

18
00:00:52,083 --> 00:00:53,500
One of you will not get one.

19
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:54,708
If you don't, you are eliminated.

20
00:00:54,875 --> 00:00:57,375
Needle, you have a win token.
Would you like to use it now?

21
00:00:57,375 --> 00:00:58,250
- Yeah!
- Announcer: Okay.

22
00:01:00,125 --> 00:01:00,583
Where is it?

23
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:01,625
There we go!

24
00:01:01,625 --> 00:01:02,416
Okay then!

25
00:01:02,416 --> 00:01:04,458
So, Ice Cube, you are at the lowest
with one vote!

26
00:01:04,666 --> 00:01:07,166
Announcer:
LLOSMMORPG voted for you.

27
00:01:07,166 --> 00:01:09,833
He was the only one.
The oddball in the group of normal voters.

28
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:13,000
There is only one cake half left,
but there are two people.

29
00:01:14,833 --> 00:01:17,125
Awkward silence...

30
00:01:17,125 --> 00:01:20,166
You know what, Coiny?
You haven't spoken once at my Cake at Stakes.

31
00:01:20,166 --> 00:01:21,958
You're just contributing to the silence.

32
00:01:21,958 --> 00:01:25,125
Coiny:
Hey, look here! I'm contributing!

33
00:01:25,125 --> 00:01:30,833
Instead of spending time on what I want to do,
I'm helping out and contributing to something else!

34
00:01:30,833 --> 00:01:33,291
[sing-song] The sound of silence!

35
00:01:34,583 --> 00:01:35,708
- Okay, so-
- Shhh!

36
00:01:35,708 --> 00:01:38,250
We have to contribute to the silence!

37
00:01:38,250 --> 00:01:39,375
- Coiny, you got-
- Shhh!

38
00:01:39,750 --> 00:01:40,291
- The per-
- Shhh!

39
00:01:40,541 --> 00:01:41,500
- Out of the final-
- Shhhh!

40
00:01:41,625 --> 00:01:42,333
Grrrr!

41
00:01:42,791 --> 00:01:43,208
Needy.

42
00:01:44,791 --> 00:01:46,458
Now that Coiny is gone, I can talk.

43
00:01:46,541 --> 00:01:47,750
Announcer:
Coiny is at five votes,

44
00:01:47,750 --> 00:01:48,250
and Needy-

45
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:49,416
is it twelve votes.

46
00:01:49,833 --> 00:01:52,708
Announcer:
Because she used her win token, she's down to six votes;

47
00:01:52,708 --> 00:01:54,583
Announcer:
but that's still the highest, so Needle is out.

48
00:01:54,583 --> 00:01:56,125
Needle: Aw, seriously?

49
00:01:56,125 --> 00:02:00,958
That proves that the number thirteen is unlucky.
Because Needle had slapped exactly thirteen times

50
00:02:00,958 --> 00:02:02,541
before she learned she was eliminated.

51
00:02:02,791 --> 00:02:05,208
Do you think Nonexistent Icy is mad at me?

52
00:02:05,416 --> 00:02:05,875
Needy!

53
00:02:06,125 --> 00:02:08,458
Yeah, I guess it's pretty big, Needy.

54
00:02:09,083 --> 00:02:10,458
Leafy:
Didn't it, Needy?!

55
00:02:10,958 --> 00:02:13,166
What's wrong with calling you Needy, Needy?!

56
00:02:13,500 --> 00:02:14,708
Don't you, Needy?!

57
00:02:15,125 --> 00:02:16,916
I love Needies!

58
00:02:17,416 --> 00:02:19,708
Do you know where she is, Needy?

59
00:02:20,208 --> 00:02:21,000
Coiny, Icy, Needy-

60
00:02:21,791 --> 00:02:23,208
[SLOWED DOWN[
Neee-

61
00:02:23,958 --> 00:02:26,458
So let's go Coiny, Icy, and Needy.

62
00:02:27,291 --> 00:02:27,541
Needy-

63
00:02:29,041 --> 00:02:29,625
...and Needy-

64
00:02:29,791 --> 00:02:30,666
is at twelve votes.

65
00:02:30,791 --> 00:02:35,666
Yeah, but, Needle, why don't you like being called Needy?

66
00:02:36,000 --> 00:02:36,291
Needy-

67
00:02:42,583 --> 00:02:43,916
Why won't it close all the way?

68
00:02:44,208 --> 00:02:48,458
What?! Can't you read?!
The carrying capacity is six!

69
00:02:48,791 --> 00:02:52,708
There are six people in there, but Spongy's kinda big.

70
00:02:52,958 --> 00:02:55,875
Oh well. In that case,
there's no room to eliminate another player.

71
00:02:56,375 --> 00:02:57,583
So, in the next contest-

72
00:02:57,583 --> 00:02:59,250
Which is?!

73
00:02:59,250 --> 00:03:00,625
I'm getting to that right now.

74
00:03:01,000 --> 00:03:06,375
Anyway, in the next contest, this contest's winning team
chooses a contestant from the contest's losing team

75
00:03:06,375 --> 00:03:09,375
to be on their team; so no one gets sent to the TLC.

76
00:03:09,625 --> 00:03:10,208
Yeah!

77
00:03:10,208 --> 00:03:14,416
Eraser:
But what is the contest?!

78
00:03:14,625 --> 00:03:15,833
Okay. Enter that room.

79
00:03:16,333 --> 00:03:18,833
Announcer:
Ha ha. I tricked you! Now you are trapped in this room.

80
00:03:19,041 --> 00:03:19,916
Announcer:
There is no way out.

81
00:03:20,125 --> 00:03:21,208
Oh no!

82
00:03:21,416 --> 00:03:24,208
Does that mean we'll starve to death in here?!

83
00:03:24,416 --> 00:03:25,750
We'll find out after the break.

84
00:03:25,875 --> 00:03:29,708
Want skin that's smooth and soft?!

85
00:03:29,708 --> 00:03:33,833
Then buy our Bubble Transformer!

86
00:03:33,833 --> 00:03:36,666
It'll turn you into a bubble,

87
00:03:36,666 --> 00:03:40,458
and Bubble's skin is super smooth!

88
00:03:40,625 --> 00:03:45,833
None of the people in our
survey said they didn't like it!

89
00:03:46,041 --> 00:03:53,666
Because they popped before we could contact them,
and we don't sell personal Bubble Recovery Centers.

90
00:03:53,666 --> 00:03:55,750
So they died...

91
00:03:55,750 --> 00:03:56,583
Euhhh...

92
00:03:56,875 --> 00:03:59,708
So yeah! Buy now!

93
00:04:00,250 --> 00:04:02,333
Everyone:
AHHHH!

94
00:04:02,333 --> 00:04:03,416
People, calm down!

95
00:04:03,916 --> 00:04:05,041
There is a way out of here.

96
00:04:05,041 --> 00:04:07,958
Liar, liar, pants of blaze!

97
00:04:08,166 --> 00:04:09,750
No, Pence-Pence, it's true.

98
00:04:10,125 --> 00:04:12,375
Only I call her Pence-Pence!

99
00:04:12,375 --> 00:04:14,375
Oh, so now you're a slapper too, aren't you?

100
00:04:14,583 --> 00:04:20,041
Hey guys, look! To pass the time, we can try to finish
these jigsaw puzzles on the floor!

101
00:04:20,041 --> 00:04:22,125
That's exactly what the seventh contest is.

102
00:04:22,291 --> 00:04:26,625
Announcer:
If your team completes your team's jigsaw puzzle,
the doors will detetct it and let you free.

103
00:04:26,958 --> 00:04:28,250
Until then, you're trapped.

104
00:04:28,541 --> 00:04:30,208
Announcer:
The fastest team wins. And go.

105
00:04:30,666 --> 00:04:32,625
This should be easy!

106
00:04:32,625 --> 00:04:35,625
Yeah! Especially because there are only nine pieces!

107
00:04:35,708 --> 00:04:37,291
'Kay, let's get going!

108
00:04:38,125 --> 00:04:42,375
You know, this is really hard because
they're all the same dark brown color!

109
00:04:42,375 --> 00:04:46,083
Something tells me we're doing something wrong!

110
00:04:46,083 --> 00:04:48,375
You worry too much, Pencil.

111
00:04:49,666 --> 00:04:50,625
Gimme that!

112
00:04:51,958 --> 00:04:53,250
Squashy Grapes:
YEEAAH!

113
00:04:53,541 --> 00:04:55,208
There's one more thing I want you to do.

114
00:04:55,208 --> 00:04:57,416
Squashy Grapes:
AHHHHH!

115
00:04:57,416 --> 00:05:01,250
Before I'll let you go, choose someone on
the Squishy Cherries to be on your team.

116
00:05:01,250 --> 00:05:04,500
Okay then, let's see who we can choose from!

117
00:05:04,791 --> 00:05:10,333
Coiny:
There's Eraser, his friend, and
the dumb jerk, and the alliance.

118
00:05:10,625 --> 00:05:11,791
Coiny:
So let's take a vote!

119
00:05:12,125 --> 00:05:13,708
Who do you want, Icy?

120
00:05:13,791 --> 00:05:14,333
Ice Cube:
Pencil!

121
00:05:14,333 --> 00:05:15,333
The rest of you?

122
00:05:15,416 --> 00:05:16,208
Everyone:
FIREY!

123
00:05:16,208 --> 00:05:19,708
Coiny:
And I don't want Firey. I guess Firey won't be the one!

124
00:05:19,833 --> 00:05:21,416
We pick Firey!

125
00:05:21,416 --> 00:05:23,333
But I hate Firey!

126
00:05:23,333 --> 00:05:25,625
Why would you do that?!

127
00:05:25,625 --> 00:05:28,791
Oh no! Now Coiny's on my team?!

128
00:05:29,500 --> 00:05:32,875
Okay, so now the Squashy Grapes
really, really outnumber the Squishy Cherries.

129
00:05:33,458 --> 00:05:35,375
Yeah, it was so funny!

130
00:05:35,666 --> 00:05:38,750
Match:
Eraser just, like, walked up and stepped on a nail!

131
00:05:38,750 --> 00:05:41,583
Hoy hoy! That's so hilar!

132
00:05:41,583 --> 00:05:46,833
But then he, like, shot up in the air,
and he so totally fell on, like, a bed of nails!

133
00:05:46,833 --> 00:05:48,625
Yeah, yeah! Wow!

134
00:05:48,625 --> 00:05:50,416
Eraser:
Hey, Match and Pencil!

135
00:05:50,416 --> 00:05:53,833
You two better not be talking about me!

136
00:05:53,833 --> 00:05:56,708
And why aren't you helping us on the puzzle anyway?

137
00:05:56,708 --> 00:05:58,541
Oh great, now you're bossy!

138
00:05:58,708 --> 00:06:02,833
I was glad when Pin, like, was eliminated,
but now you're like her!

139
00:06:02,833 --> 00:06:05,375
Eraser:
I just wanna finish the puzzle, okay?

140
00:06:05,583 --> 00:06:06,416
Sure...

141
00:06:06,666 --> 00:06:07,416
Huuh... Yeh...

142
00:06:07,416 --> 00:06:08,208
GUYS!

143
00:06:08,208 --> 00:06:10,458
All the pieces are upside down!

144
00:06:10,541 --> 00:06:12,791
The brown goes on the back!

145
00:06:12,791 --> 00:06:14,208
Eraser:
Ohh, no wonder!

146
00:06:14,375 --> 00:06:17,875
So yeah, Cherries, keep working.
Because you're still trapped in this room.

147
00:06:17,875 --> 00:06:19,666
And that means no voting for this episode!

148
00:06:19,916 --> 00:06:24,000
However, episode eight will still come out on August 1st, and there will be voting then!

149
00:06:24,708 --> 00:06:27,916
Hey! I found two pieces that fir together!

150
00:06:27,916 --> 00:06:29,833
- Pencil: Finally!
- Eraser: It's about time!